cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived data, please cite the preregistration and this repository."
title: "ortho-tech-diffusion: detecting and adjudicating concept emergence in the orthopaedic literature"
abstract: >-
  Pipeline and protocol for a preregistered discovery study distinguishing the emergence of
  terminology from the emergence of concepts in the procedural orthopaedic literature
  (PubMed/MEDLINE, 2005-2025). Provides a locally verified mirror of the PubMed baseline and
  update files, a parallel parser producing an analytic table with explicit PubMed/MEDLINE
  status flags, PMID deduplication honouring DeleteCitation, programmatic expansion of the
  MeSH subtree defining the field, n-gram canonicalisation, a take-off detector yielding a
  year of emergence per term, strength axes based on concentration rather than counts, and
  predecessor-candidate generation supporting a manual substitution test. Terms are coded
  into five categories: novel concept, renaming, conceptual evolution, measurement artifact,
  non-technological term. Protocol, coding manual and freeze manifest in docs/protocol/.
